  "caption": "Quinn discovered the sauna, stayed 40 minutes, became soup, and then wondered if it could replace leg day.\n\nRegular sauna use is linked with heart-health benefits in large studies, and heat may ease muscle soreness, but research can't yet prove cause and effect. It's an add-on to training, not a swap.\n\nWhat can help: keeping sessions to 10–20 minutes, hydrating before and after, going in rested rather than dehydrated, skipping alcohol, leaving if you feel dizzy or queasy, and standing up slowly.\n\nCheck with your doctor first if you have a heart or blood pressure condition or are pregnant, and avoid heat on a fresh injury for the first day or two.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
